 ],
 "literal": "Like a sapphire vessel filled with honey / in the narrow-mouthed mountain pool, the wide-mouthed toad / croaks like a flat rattle-drum, in the land of the lord. / Under the long white moonlight of the former moon, / he embraced, indeed, my long shoulders. / Today, the jasmine buds smell sweet.",
 "translation": "The lord of the land where wide-mouthed toads croak like flat rattle-drums in narrow-mouthed mountain pools that look like sapphire vessels filled with sweet honey, once embraced my long shoulders under the long, white light of the full moon. Today, the jasmine buds are fragrant.",
 "modern": "தேன் நிரப்பிய நீலமணிக் கிண்ணத்தைப் போன்ற குறுகிய வாயையுடைய சுனையில், அகன்ற வாயையுடைய தேரையானது தட்டைப் பறையைப் போல ஒலிக்கின்ற நாட்டின் தலைவன், முன்பு ஒரு காலத்தில் முழு நிலவின் நீண்ட வெண்மையான நிலவொளியில் என் நீண்ட தோள்களைத் தழுவினான். ஆனால் இன்றோ, முல்லை அரும்புகள் மணம் வீசுகின்றன.",
 "explanation": "The heroine is speaking to her friend or expressing her grief to herself upon the arrival of the rainy season. The hero had promised to return by the time the jasmine buds bloom, but he has not yet arrived. She recalls how he once embraced her long shoulders under the bright, white moonlight of a past month. The imagery of the wide-mouthed toad croaking like a flat rattle-drum in a narrow mountain pool, which resembles a sapphire vessel filled with honey, vividly evokes the onset of the rains in the mullai landscape. Now, as the jasmine buds begin to spread their sweet fragrance, her loneliness and longing are intensified by his absence.",
